Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||05-29-2000||08:24 PM||||I created a simple business card for my website (The Fiero Project), and got several sheets of them printed and laminated. I leave them on Fieros I see, so the owner can visit my site and find Fiero resources such as this Forum.. <P>After the first batch, I've made some revisions to the design.. I'm going to use thicker paper next time, and thicker plastic for the laminations. That way they'll hold up better.. Although right now they can be completely submerged in water (eg. rain) and not get get blurred..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||05-29-2000||08:36 PM||||For those of you who don't know me, or my site.. the Fiero Project is a website of Fiero resources, such as a gallery of Fiero pictures, <I>(more are always welcome! I have a few to add, but I'm going to start a new gallery page so I'm waiting until I have more..)</I>, Fiero links, lots of modifications, a bookstore (courtesy of the Barnes & Noble affiliate program) and more..<P>Check it out.. <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/</A> <P><BR>sorry for the sales pitch.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
